      <h2>4. Using Online Conversation to Practice Communication</h2>

      <p>Online voice and video platforms can provide another environment for practicing conversation. The main benefit is not that the platform automatically creates confidence, but that it can give users opportunities to communicate with people they do not already know.</p>

      <h3>4.1 Voice and Video Practice</h3>

      <p>Voice conversations allow you to practice tone, pacing and listening. Video adds visual communication such as facial expressions and eye contact.</p>

      <h3>4.2 Low-Commitment Conversations</h3>

      <p>A short conversation can be easier to approach than a long social event. Users can focus on practicing one skill at a time rather than trying to perform perfectly.</p>

      <h3>4.3 Boundaries Still Matter</h3>

      <p>Anonymity or limited profile information does not remove the need for online safety. Avoid sharing sensitive information and leave conversations that become inappropriate or uncomfortable.</p>

      <h3>4.4 Know What the Platform Actually Provides</h3>

      <p>Before using any online chat service, review its current privacy policy, community guidelines and available moderation controls. Features can change over time, so users should rely on the platform's current documentation rather than assumptions.</p>

